{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fleet/tests/postgres.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:15:47.944539Z","id":"3e878bdbfa061840541a63d7ffbdde07d3bc46cd8da92c32838f6a64375ec149","body":{"detail":"Every test here is ignored without CLAX_TEST_PG_URL, and none was run when the PostgreSQL backend was written: the SQL of crates/clax-fleet/src/coord.rs (PgCoordinator), pages.rs, content.rs and pg.rs (migrate, Fence::check) is checked only by compiling. Run `CLAX_TEST_PG_URL=postgresql://... just fleet-pg-test` before relying on the backend.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"60daf0c695e6bb08c729a3ef1c3632bb363fbe36ce1cfd02c39f086c773b42bf"},"summary":"The PostgreSQL tests have not run against a server on this branch","tags":["test-coverage","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fleet/tests/leases.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:03.388970Z","id":"53716d70f02c354778848cbcc5c8085402b845c85264c7db334a42a840fa8d15","body":{"detail":"MemCoordinator (crates/clax-fleet/src/coord.rs:255-374) cannot fail a call, so no test reaches Fleet::renew's error arm (RENEW_FAILURES, fleet.rs:633-637) or the heartbeat failure that turns /readyz to 503 (fleet.rs:571-574). No test holds a stop in progress to check that a request then gets 503 'is moving' and does not start the instance again (Slot::stopping, fleet.rs:341-343), the behaviour cef687699 added. Every leases.rs test runs Storage::Disk (crates/clax-fleet/tests/common.rs:65), a combination production never uses; the Storage::Postgres arm of Fleet::open (fleet.rs:489-520: PgPages, PgContent, PgAppData under MovingAppData, Core::start_on) and crates/clax-fleet/src/app_data.rs have no test at all, not even among the ignored PostgreSQL tests (tests/postgres.rs opens a Store directly). The existing record on tests/postgres.rs covers the PostgreSQL tests not having run, not these gaps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"a7f169d2a802625d8f93ffdcf4e7ea126eb1030ebfceb590157f74c03396af34"},"suggested_fix":"Give MemCoordinator a failure switch (fail the next N calls, or all of them while set) and test that a held instance stops after RENEW_FAILURES failed ticks and that /readyz answers 503 while heartbeats fail; test a request during a stop by holding the slot through a Coordinator whose release blocks on a channel; make Storage::Postgres's page and content stores injectable (a PageStore/ContentStore factory) so a leases test can run Fleet::open over clax_pagevfs::MemPages and MemContent, including an app data call.","summary":"The lease paths that keep one owner per instance under failure are untested: renewal errors, refusal while stopping, and the PostgreSQL storage's open path","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","correctness","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fleet/tests/leases.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:24.244787Z","id":"1b14ec92b60a52f719eebedc28bef6a80e135e8679caee898b8b18499d7bb29b","body":{"detail":"MemCoordinator's methods all return Ok (crates/clax-fleet/src/coord.rs:255-374); it is the only Coordinator besides PgCoordinator. crates/clax-fleet/tests/common.rs:65 hard-codes `storage: Storage::Disk`, the only Fleet::new in tests (common.rs:56), while production pairs leases with Postgres only (crates/clax-fleet/src/main.rs:231). `grep -rn 'Storage::Postgres|PgAppData|is moving|RENEW_FAILURES|readyz' crates/clax-fleet/tests/*.rs` finds nothing; crates/clax-fleet/src/app_data.rs has no #[test]. leases.rs tests (lines 47, 85, 109, 136, 154) cover hashing, drain, live lease, lost lease, out-of-hops; postgres.rs tests (28, 43, 75, 119, 168) open Store/PgCoordinator/content directly, not Fleet::open.","kind":"comment","references":"53716d70f02c354778848cbcc5c8085402b845c85264c7db334a42a840fa8d15","summary":"confirmed: no test reaches renew errors, the stopping refusal, or the Postgres arm of Fleet::open and PgAppData","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fleet/tests/leases.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:00:21.356591Z","id":"e3434db3ef8ba6792ff0bac5513546c65f9a2b3becf96c2545946a6884952a91","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"53716d70f02c354778848cbcc5c8085402b845c85264c7db334a42a840fa8d15","summary":"Partly addressed in git:347050368: MemCoordinator::fail now fails every call, and tests cover renewal failures (leases::an_instance_stops_once_its_renewals_have_failed_long_enough, which also checks ready() turns false), paused instances and forged headers; tests/postgres.rs an_instance_moves_between_processes_with_its_data runs Storage::Postgres (needs CLAX_TEST_PG_URL). Still untested: a request during a stop in progress answering 503 'is moving' (Slot::stopping), which needs a stop held open.","tags":["session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
